AArch64 GussetParkWakeDekker
"AArch64 litmus specification of Gusset's shared-memory completion ring
 park/wake Dekker protocol (`crates/gusset/src/pool/ring.rs::try_publish` +
 `take_waiter` vs `ticket_reader.go::waitRing`).

 Verification note: verified under `herd7` (`aarch64.cat`, verdict `Never`) in
 the nightly `formal` CI job, and mirrored by `crates/gusset/tests/aarch64_litmus_model.rs`
 which executes the `aarch64.cat` / `aarch64hwreqs.cat` relational consistency
 check over all candidate `(rf, co)` executions under `cargo test` and asserts
 syntactic parity with this file.

 P0 (Rust worker): publishes slot sequence `seq = 1` with STLR, executes
 `fence(SeqCst)` (`DMB ISH`), reads `waiting` (`LDR`), and when non-zero swaps
 `waiting` to 0 (`SWPAL`).

 P1 (Go reader `waitRing` on LSE / ARMv8.1+): announces parking via
 `atomic.SwapUint32(&waiting, 1)` (`SWPAL W0, W2, [X1]`, with `X1 = waiting`) and
 re-checks `ringReady()` via `atomic.LoadUint64(&seq)` (`LDAR X4, [X3]`, with `X3 = seq`).

 Safety condition (`Never` under `aarch64.cat`):
   0:X2=0 (worker observed waiting == 0 and skipped writing pipe wake token)
   /\ 1:X4=0 (reader observed seq == 0 and parked on the pipe)

 Companion disproof variants exercised in `crates/gusset/tests/aarch64_litmus_model.rs`:
   1. `STLRW` + `LDAPR` (FEAT_LRCPC RCpc acquire-pc load): `[W & L]; po; [R & Q]`
      is NOT in `bob` (`aarch64hwreqs.cat` line 134 only covers `[W & L]; po; [R & A]`),
      yielding a consistent `ob`-acyclic lost-wake execution (`Sometimes`).
   2. `STR` + `LDAR` (missing release on `waiting = 1`): `Sometimes`.
   3. Worker omitting `DMB ISH` before `LDR W2, [waiting]`: `Sometimes`."
{
  uint64_t seq = 0;
  uint32_t waiting = 0;
  0:X0=1; 0:X1=seq; 0:X3=waiting; 0:X4=0;
  1:X0=1; 1:X1=waiting; 1:X3=seq;
}
 P0                       | P1                       ;
 STLR X0, [X1]            | SWPAL W0, W2, [X1]       ;
 DMB ISH                  | LDAR X4, [X3]            ;
 LDR W2, [X3]             |                          ;
 CBNZ W2, L_claim         |                          ;
 B L_done                 |                          ;
L_claim:                  |                          ;
 SWPAL W4, W5, [X3]       |                          ;
L_done:                   |                          ;
exists (0:X2=0 /\ 1:X4=0)
